<project>
This is a Simplified Chinese OCR application built in Python.
It captures screen regions, runs OCR, applies NLP post-processing, and exports EPUB files.
The app is designed for extensibility — new features slot in without modifying existing code.
Developer hardware: RTX 4070 Laptop (8 GB VRAM), i7-13700HX, 32 GB RAM.
Full architecture: @docs/app_guidelines.md
Full OCR pipeline reference: @docs/ocr_guidelines.md
Current work queue: @docs/NEXT_STEPS.md
Architecture decisions: @docs/DECISIONS.md
</project>

<architecture>
- Framework: PySide6 (not PyQt6). Use PySide6 imports everywhere.
- Screen capture: mss library only. Never pyautogui or PIL.grab for screen capture.
- Global hotkeys: pynput. Hotkey listener runs in a separate thread — use Qt signals to cross into the main thread. Never call GUI methods directly from the hotkey thread.
- OCR engine: PaddleOCR (PP-OCRv5). paddlepaddle-gpu installed from official PaddlePaddle index, not PyPI.
- EPUB output: ebooklib.
- Git operations (automated): gitpython. Developer workflow uses Windsurf Source Control panel.
- OpenRouter API: openai library with base_url="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1".
- Local LLM API: openai library with base_url="http://localhost:11434/v1" (Ollama).
</architecture>

<extensibility>
Every major subsystem uses the Registrable registry pattern (core/registry.py).
New implementations subclass the ABC and set name="identifier". They self-register on import.
Never use if/elif chains to select between OCR engines, pipeline stages, or output formats.
Always use the registry: OCREngine.get(config["ocr_engine"])().
Pipeline stages are defined as ordered name lists in PIPELINE_MODES dict — not hardcoded logic.
New pipeline modes = add one entry to PIPELINE_MODES. No other changes.
All cross-module communication goes through core/event_bus.py. No direct imports between modules.
modules/ directory contains stubs only. Do NOT implement translation, manga, web_scraper, or story_memory unless explicitly instructed.
</extensibility>

<vram>
VRAM tier is set by config["vram_tier"]: "8gb" (default) or "16gb".
VRAMManager (core/vram_manager.py) tracks allocations. Every model must call allocate() before loading and release() after unloading.
Never hardcode model names. Read from config — defaults are set by vram_tier.
8gb tier: MacBERT-base (~2GB), Qwen2.5-7B Q4_K_M (~5GB), BGE-M3 (~1.1GB).
16gb tier: MacBERT-large (~4GB), Qwen2.5-14B Q4_K_M (~10GB), BGE-M3 resident.
FORBIDDEN on 8gb: loading PaddleOCR + any 7B+ LLM simultaneously. Will OOM.
Always unload PaddleOCR before loading any LLM or large BERT model.
</vram>

<correctness>
CRITICAL — Folder and image ordering MUST be numeric, never lexicographic.
CORRECT:   sorted(items, key=lambda x: int(x))
FORBIDDEN: sorted(items) or os.listdir() without explicit numeric sort.
Lexicographic sort produces: 1, 10, 11, 2, 3 — a fatal ordering bug.
EPUB chapter spine must be built in the same numeric order.
Image filenames within folders use zero-padded integers: 0001.png, 0002.png, etc.
</correctness>

<environment>
Python 3.11 only. conda environment named "chinese-ocr".
opencv installed via conda-forge (not pip opencv-python — causes Qt conflict with PySide6).
paddlepaddle-gpu installed via: pip install paddlepaddle-gpu==3.0.0 -i https://www.paddlepaddle.org.cn/packages/stable/cu126/
Do NOT use uv to install paddlepaddle-gpu (wheel naming conflict).
All other packages via pip inside the conda env.
</environment>

<workflow>
Always present a plan for approval before writing code for any non-trivial change.
After completing a ticket, ask to update NEXT_STEPS.md and CHANGELOG.md.
Commit format: [TICKET-ID] Brief description. Example: [ARCH-001] Implement registry pattern.
Feature branches: feature/ARCH-001, feature/FEAT-capture, etc. Merge to dev, not main.
main branch = stable only. dev branch = active development.
Run pytest after each change. Fix failures before moving to the next file.
</workflow>

<coding>
Type hints on all function signatures.
Docstrings on all public classes and methods (one-line is fine for simple methods).
No bare except: clauses. Catch specific exceptions.
Logging via utils/logging_config.py — never print() for operational messages.
Config access via utils/config_manager.py dotted-key API — never open config.json directly.
Test files mirror source structure: tests/ocr/test_engine.py mirrors ocr/engines/paddle_engine.py.
The numeric sort P0 test must exist: tests/utils/test_file_utils.py::test_numeric_sort_never_lexicographic.
</coding>
